{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.cerberauth.com/identity-provider/draft/2024-09/provider.schema.json",
  "name": "Casdoor",
  "abstract": "Open-source identity and access management platform written in Go, with a web UI. Acts as an OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML, CAS, LDAP, RADIUS and SCIM identity provider, with password, email and SMS code, WebAuthn and passkey sign-in, 70+ built-in social providers and TOTP, WebAuthn, email and SMS multi-factor authentication. Supports multiple organizations per instance, each with its own users, groups, roles, applications and branding, and Casbin-based ACL, RBAC and ABAC permissions. Positioned as an agent-first IAM that exposes its management API as an MCP server and acts as an OAuth 2.1 authorization server for MCP servers. Self-hosted as a single Go binary with a SQL database under Apache-2.0, or managed on Casdoor Cloud.",
